Curt Varga tightened his throat muscles as he whispered his questions to his brother in the small, covered booth across the room.  
"Do you suspect you are working with me?" he asked. "If so, we must end this arrangement; I can't ruin your career either."  
A tiny speaker hidden under the bone at his right temple vibrated softly from the laughter that mocked him.  
"I think they do, Falcon," Val Varga said lightly. "But it doesn't matter; someone has to do the undercover work—and I can do it with the least suspicion."  
His voice softened. "Careers aren't important. I remember Dad had a good reputation as a biochemist until the Food Administrators thought his work threatened their control. And as a Commander of the IP, you were set to go higher."  
Curt Varga grinned, and suddenly all the harshness disappeared from his tan face. Only laughter appeared in his cool gray eyes and a hint of adventurous swagger in the tilt of his head, showing the man.

