Miles was a very small boy, so his dad’s friend said he should be called “Inches” instead of Miles.  The family were from America, but Inches was born in Assam, a region in India.  When he was four, he had never been to another country.  

Assam is a kingdom in India.  It is west of China and south of the huge Himalaya Mountains.  On clear days you can see some of the mountains from Inches’s home.  

One early morning, Inches woke up and shouted in Assamese, “Tezzan, take me.”  Tezzan is a word for a helper in Assam.  He came right away, dressed Inches, and gave him a slice of dry toast and a plantain for breakfast.  Then he held Inches’s hand and they began their usual morning walk.

