Tool Call: compute_grade_level with args {'text': 'Augmented reality (AR) is a new way to look at the world around us. When we use AR, we see real things like the street or a playground, but we also see extra pictures or sounds that come from a computer. The computer adds things like a map, a game, or a countdown timer to help us understand what is happening. AR does not replace the real world. It just makes it easier to see more information. For example, when you watch a soccer game on TV, AR can put the score on the screen so you can see it while you watch the game.\n\nAR uses a special camera on your phone or a headset. The camera looks at the real world and the computer finds objects in the picture. Then the computer puts new information right next to the objects. That information could be a label, a voice, or a picture. AR is also used to help us learn or to do work that is hard to do with just the real world. AR is a fast-growing technology that many people will use in the future.'}
