When they stepped into the open they almost fell because they were amazed. A huge gray horse, its tail hair made the water look wavy, was drinking from the pool. The ripples around its face looked like melted gold. On the horse's back sat an old white-haired man in a loose shiny chainmail coat. He had no hat, and a round iron helmet hung from his saddle. His reins were red leather, five or six inches deep, scalloped at the edges. His high padded saddle had red straps and a red leather belt.

"Look!" said Una, as if Dan wasn't staring straight at her. "It's like the picture in your room—'Sir Isumbras at the Ford'."

