 Horn returned to his kingdom, but he had not yet punished Fikenhild, the traitor who had separated him from Rimenhild. Aylmer had told him about this. Horn also had to deal with King Modi, who wanted to marry Rimenhild against her will.

When Horn was about to rescue Rimenhild from King Modi, Fikenhild ran away. But he still planned to hurt others. He bribed many knights to follow him. He built a big stone castle on a rock surrounded by water so that it was hard to attack.

One night, he and Rimenhild secretly left and married in the castle. They held a big feast at sunrise to celebrate.

Horn had no idea about this because he only heard rumors. But in a dream he saw Rimenhild. She looked like a shipwrecked sailor, calling his name. When she tried to swim to him, Fikenhild appeared and stopped her.

