During this time a cheerful woodcutter named Arthur‑a‑Bland lived in Nottingham. No squire in the town could challenge him, and nobody would ask him to stop unless he chose to. He carried a long pole on his shoulder, and he could move through crowds so easily that everyone stepped aside.

One summer morning Arthur‑a‑Bland went into Sherwood Forest to watch the deer. While he was there, he met Robin Hood. When Robin saw him, he decided to have some fun and asked him to stand up.

“Who are you, friend, that you come here so boldly?” Robin asked. “You look like a thief trying to steal the king’s meat. I’m a ranger in the forest, and the king has given me the job of protecting the deer. That’s why I have to ask you to stop.”

