 After dinner, the table was ready for Katy to clean up. The family went to the living room to talk about a walk in the woods for flowers that we promised the children for that afternoon. Suddenly we heard heavy steps in the hallway going into the dining room. "Run, Willy," said mom, "and see what’s making that noise." Willy ran out, came back laughing so hard he could barely talk. "It’s old Charley," he said. "He’s in the dining room." We all ran to the door, and sure enough, Charley was there, eating from the plates. We laughed at him standing there, as if it were his own stall and manger! We wanted Charley to have what was left, but it didn’t feel right to have a horse in the house, and we feared he might knock over the dishes.

