The watchman paced back and forth. I couldn't hear him well from under the tarp. Sometimes when he was far away, I couldn't hear him at all. After a long time without hearing him, I peeped out carefully. It seemed like what Biddy had said was true. The watchman was sitting in an old armchair made of ironbound cotton bales. He had his long coat tucked between his legs, his hat over his nose, and he was fast asleep.

