About 600 B.C., Greek towns in a region called Ionia were the smartest and most important places in Greece. They were also the best traders on the sea in the Mediterranean. The town of Miletus, at the very south, was the richest town and the main focus of the early Greek age, called the “Ionian awakening.” This was the start of ancient Greek culture and the birth of Greek philosophy.

