 Texas was a name that many people did not understand well. Some thought it went to the Rio Grande, others thought it stopped at the Nueces River. Most people saw the Rio Grande as the border with Mexico. Ned and his friends felt the same. They were on land that could belong to Mexico, but they, the Texans, were fighting for it. They were not born in Texas, but they loved it. People elsewhere argued about whether their fight was right or wrong. They knew they had to fight for their lives and for the homes they had built in the wild, hoping for promises that had not been kept. That was the only answer for them. Seeing Texas, green and full of forests along the streams, made Ned happy. The rough frontier men in buckskins who rode with him were the men he had chosen.

